'bellman equation', 'bijan khezri', "i'll", "i've", "i'm", 'afterthought', 'application', 'appropriate', 'approximate', 'approximately', 'articulation', 'associations', 'categorical', 'communicate', 'computation', 'computational', 'conditionally', 'consequence', 'consideration', 'considering', 'constituting', 'construction', 'customization', 'derivations', 'description', 'descriptions', 'development', 'discussions', 'distinction', 'distinguishing', 'distribution', 'educationally', 'efficiently', 'elaborating', 'environment', 'expectation', 'formulation', 'formulations', 'fundamental', 'generalization', 'hierarchical', 'independent', 'inferential', 'information', 'ingredients', 'interaction', 'interactive', 'interesting', 'justification', 'mathematical', 'mathematically', 'minimization', 'misconceptions', 'necessarily', 'observables', 'observation', 'observations', 'parameterize', 'parameterizes', 'perspective', 'possibilities', 'possibility', 'presentation', 'probabilistic', 'psychological', 'relationships', 'simulations', 'sophisticated', 'specifically', 'statistical', 'statistically', 'supplementary', 'symmetrical', 'temperature', 'terminology', 'trajectories', 'uncertainty', 'variational'], 'boost_param': 'low', 'filter_profanity': False, 'redact_pii': False, 'redact_pii_audio': False, 'redact_pii_audio_quality': None, 'redact_pii_policies': None, 'redact_pii_sub': None, 'speaker_labels': True, 'content_safety': False, 'iab_categories': True, 'content_safety_labels': {'status': 'unavailable', 'results': [], 'summary': {}}, 'iab_categories_result': {'status': 'success', 'results': [{'text': "You. Hello and welcome everyone. It's Active Inference guest stream number 48.1 on July 19, 2023. We're here with Arthur Giuliani and Adam Safron, also joined by Michael Edward Johnson in discussion. We're going to have a presentation and then a conversation about deep canals, a deep learning approach to refining the cannilization theory of psychopathology. So thank you all for joining and looking forward to this presentation and discussion. Thanks Daniel.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5405477285385132, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.3252016007900238, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.06309625506401062, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.01880001276731491, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01588524505496025, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.004942483268678188, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Dating'}, {'relevance': 0.004732124973088503, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.004698548465967178, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.00391694949939847, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0021329019218683243, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4200, 'end': 41764}, 'sentences_idx_start': 0, 'sentences_idx_end': 6}, {'text': "I'm very happy to be here with Admin Mike to talk about this work and to discuss more broadly this general direction that's emerged over the past few years to try to utilize some of the concepts from the active inference world and computational modeling more generally to understand what's going on both in psychopathology and in psychedelic therapy. Yeah, so I'll give a brief presentation and we'll move into a kind of more general discussion of this work.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6803452372550964, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.47334372997283936, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.29634904861450195, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.06031055748462677, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.05873630940914154, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.014956854283809662, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.013817783445119858, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.011420653201639652, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.010089901275932789, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.003149278461933136, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 41812, 'end': 76630}, 'sentences_idx_start': 7, 'sentences_idx_end': 8}, {'text': "It'll start with some kind of general considerations around psychedelic therapy, some of the neuroscience of psychedelics, and then move kind of more specifically into the model. So there is this class of drugs, these serotonergic psychedelic drugs, which include psilocybin, DMT, LSD and others. And the past decade has seen a resurgence of interest in psychedelic therapy, psychedelic assisted psychotherapy, where one or multiple of these drugs is used in conjunction with a kind of psychotherapeutic protocol.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5042388439178467, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.40451255440711975, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.12047040462493896, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0870405063033104, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.03670378401875496, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.011460009030997753, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.008345148526132107, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.006392714101821184, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005821085534989834, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.004334674216806889, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 79800, 'end': 117280}, 'sentences_idx_start': 9, 'sentences_idx_end': 11}, {'text': "And there's been a lot of investment of money and time and clinical resources into utilizing these drugs for treatments depression, anxiety disorders, substance use disorders and others. And there seems to be quite a lot of positive signals suggesting that these kinds of therapeutic interventions can actually be quite effective. So there's a number of studies suggesting that psilocybin assisted psychotherapy can be helpful for depression, anxiety, substance use disorder and others.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5231695771217346, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.48663103580474854, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.4006248414516449, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.33733752369880676, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.004813716281205416, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.003834177041426301, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.0034801780711859465, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.003305097809061408, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>SmokingCessation'}, {'relevance': 0.003048836486414075, 'label': 'HealthyLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.0017658401047810912, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 118180, 'end': 155230}, 'sentences_idx_start': 12, 'sentences_idx_end': 14}, {'text': 'And as this work advances, there are more and more larger clinical trials comparing it for example, to the standard treatments with SSRIs, with multiple studies suggesting that pilocybin assisted psychotherapy is at least as effective as the Lexapro kind of standard of care. All of this seems to suggest, and the timelines are kind of pointing at this idea, that psilocybin treatment for major depressive disorder may be only a couple of years away from becoming approved as an actual treatment in the United States.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7783923745155334, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.2220517247915268, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.12150417268276215, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.04730239510536194, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.009419763460755348, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.005795010831207037, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004861136432737112, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>PharmaceuticalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0038254265673458576, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.003168229479342699, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.002147204475477338, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 155920, 'end': 205460}, 'sentences_idx_start': 15, 'sentences_idx_end': 16}, {'text': "Which means that it's quite important for us to understand what's going on mechanistically in the brain so that these kinds of treatments can be best optimized, best determined how to be used for which kinds of mental issues people might be having, and under what kinds of treatment protocols we might expect the most success. I think this will also ultimately, hopefully lead to the development of even better drugs, even better treatment protocols and much more personalized care.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.961897611618042, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.8732839226722717, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.19616377353668213, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.06052670255303383, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.01872936263680458, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.012426833622157574, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.012067119590938091, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.006740327458828688, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.005701207555830479, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.003372705541551113, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 206150, 'end': 248480}, 'sentences_idx_start': 17, 'sentences_idx_end': 18}, {'text': "So some of the basics of how these drugs work on the brain for those who are unfamiliar, so these are the serotonergic psychedelics. They are serotonergic because they act as agonists for a number of serotonin receptors in the brain and the central nervous system. More broadly, it's thought that most specifically these drugs like psilocybin work through agonizing, the serotonin five H T two A receptor.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.06685403734445572, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.02221846953034401, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.016526665538549423, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.003901514457538724, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0031961589120328426, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>PharmaceuticalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0021858145482838154, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.0016499229241162539, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0014830303844064474, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0009307558066211641, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0005996318650431931, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 251940, 'end': 283160}, 'sentences_idx_start': 19, 'sentences_idx_end': 21}, {'text': "And this has been demonstrated multiple times by using blockers antagonists of the five H T two A receptor which seem to largely remove the effect of psilocybin or other psychedelic drugs. And what this two A receptor does when it's agonized is it excites the neuron, making it more likely to fire. And this is kind of essential to some of the downstream effects.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.026570487767457962, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.011334313079714775, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.008836949244141579, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.005287567153573036, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.0026339490432292223, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0015691067092120647, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.001540578086860478, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0014332107966765761, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>PharmaceuticalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0014287892263382673, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.001372135360725224, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 284860, 'end': 315780}, 'sentences_idx_start': 22, 'sentences_idx_end': 24}, {'text': 'So given that it seems that this two way receptor that psychedelics are mainly targeting, the question then becomes well, where in the brain are these two A receptors? Most widely expressed? And research has focused on, I would say, three kind of key areas over the past decade or so. The first being the thalamus, which is a region involved in the gating of sensory information into the cortex.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.188969686627388, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.07360228896141052, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.015805844217538834, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.006876674480736256, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.004621228203177452, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0026734191924333572, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0016303345328196883, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.001532056019641459, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.0014687554212287068, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0012016668915748596, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 317800, 'end': 345340}, 'sentences_idx_start': 25, 'sentences_idx_end': 28}, {'text': "There's a lot of expression in the cortex itself, expression for example, in the visual system, which is perhaps not surprising given the prevalence of visual hallucinations and psychedelic use. But therapeutically a lot of focus has been on the prefrontal cortex where there is also a dense expression of these receptors. And then also more recent work has looked at the claustrom which is a small brain region responsible for coordinating the transition dynamics of cortical activation. And this too is likely of central importance to the psychedelic effect.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8275479078292847, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.13665850460529327, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.027280747890472412, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.024852558970451355, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0029738149605691433, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.0024363594129681587, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0021998619195073843, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.001662431051954627, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.001280536875128746, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0012598315952345729, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 345680, 'end': 386170}, 'sentences_idx_start': 29, 'sentences_idx_end': 32}, {'text': 'So kind of moving up one level of abstraction to fMRI studies, there are a few kind of like key takeaways which have been identified from a few different fMRI studies looking at psychedelic use. Kind of the main theme has largely been this idea of increased entropy or increased complexity of the cortical activation in the brain. So there are various measures of this.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3002459406852722, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.04827884957194328, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.02140895649790764, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.018033454194664955, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.009422989562153816, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.007830148562788963, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.003576240735128522, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0025799984578043222, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.002223716815933585, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.001290690852329135, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 390080, 'end': 421690}, 'sentences_idx_start': 33, 'sentences_idx_end': 35}, {'text': "On the right here there's a figure of one of the common measures of complexity and looking at various different kinds of states that an individual might be in and how that relates to complexity. So you have individuals in vegetative states or anesthesized states having relatively low brain activity complexity, you have individuals in awake states having higher complexity and then individuals who have ingested either psilocybin or LSD showing the highest brain complexity.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8954834938049316, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.20125973224639893, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0207976084202528, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0032393441069871187, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0018923727329820395, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0015830760821700096, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0011708399979397655, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.00099641690030694, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0008818060159683228, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.0008444568375125527, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 423180, 'end': 460340}, 'sentences_idx_start': 36, 'sentences_idx_end': 37}, {'text': "Now, along with this, rather than just this kind of like single unified score, there's work looking particularly at the changes in functional connectivity between different brain regions or different brain networks. And the general trend seems to be that you have decreased within network functional connectivity and increase between network functional connectivity, which this kind of can be interpreted as different brain networks which typically don't communicate as much with each.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6883310675621033, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00822977814823389, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0046776956878602505, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0014395089820027351, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.001247246633283794, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0010619718814268708, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0010349364019930363, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0008917060331441462, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0008690124959684908, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0007417139713652432, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 462680, 'end': 491808}, 'sentences_idx_start': 38, 'sentences_idx_end': 39}, {'text': 'Other, more likely to communicate with each other undo the effects of psychedelics and the kind of like internal coherence of networks is reduced under psychedelics. People have maybe heard of this default mode network right, which is responsible for a lot of self referential processing which is responsible, which is typically activated, for example, when individuals are off task, mind wandering, not actively engaged.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2762243151664734, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.02682117186486721, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004492912441492081, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0043535660952329636, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.002085792599245906, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0019028028473258018, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.001064453972503543, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.000906325236428529, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0008603016030974686, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.0007883199141360819, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 491814, 'end': 521400}, 'sentences_idx_start': 40, 'sentences_idx_end': 41}, {'text': "The default mode network has been kind of consistently implicated in being having less of this kind of like within network connectivity, less of this functional integration. And this has been hypothesized to be one of the kind of key mechanisms of the therapeutic effect of psychedelics. In addition to looking at kind of like brain network activity on a high level, you can then also zoom in much more deeply and look at what's actually going on at the neuron by neuron level or the neuron connectivity level.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.444162517786026, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.2433747500181198, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.007153289392590523, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0038012589793652296, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0037586460821330547, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0020973205100744963, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0013628891902044415, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.001260574092157185, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0011717884335666895, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.00116253225132823, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 522940, 'end': 561030}, 'sentences_idx_start': 42, 'sentences_idx_end': 44}, {'text': "Here we see kind of very certain, very consistent story around this psychoplastogenic effect or this neuroplastogenic effect, where there are a number of different markers of increased plasticity in the brain. So one that's very common is this increased brain derived neurotropic factor which we see hours after psychedelic use for a variety of different psychedelic drugs. And this is then accompanied a few hours later by visible increases in the dendritic spine growth in cortical parameter neurons.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8946250081062317, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.03214891254901886, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.009563865140080452, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.009557846933603287, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.001612457213923335, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0014757419703528285, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0012729306472465396, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0012141966726630926, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.0009873652597889304, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.0008896183571778238, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 562680, 'end': 607568}, 'sentences_idx_start': 45, 'sentences_idx_end': 47}, {'text': "So this is both the number of dendritic spines and the complexity of the spines. You can see a very clear example of this here on the right, where you have on the top the vehicle and then the bottom the DMT treated pyramidal neuron. And the difference is very stark. You don't even have to do any sort of actual computational analysis for it to be clear that there's quite significant dendritic growth from a single dosing.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2767144441604614, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.15205499529838562, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0068017239682376385, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>ThyroidDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0029020814690738916, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.0019368218490853906, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00028168255812488496, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.00028123147785663605, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0002799748908728361, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TelecommunicationsIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00027859507827088237, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Ear,NoseAndThroatConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.00020908992155455053, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 607744, 'end': 639980}, 'sentences_idx_start': 48, 'sentences_idx_end': 51}, {'text': "And the changes to functional connectivity, which I mentioned in the previous slide, tend to persist, though in a less extreme form than what we see during the acute effects. So the question then becomes, given all of this, how can we attempt to tell a consistent computational story, what's actually going on during both the acute effects, the post acute effects, and in terms of the actual downstream therapeutic outcomes?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9394971132278442, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.024252351373434067, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Injuries'}, {'relevance': 0.005960206966847181, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.005497063510119915, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0042232731357216835, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}, {'relevance': 0.0025669338647276163, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.002375169424340129, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0023535473737865686, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0016047828830778599, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0012855557724833488, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>LungAndRespiratoryHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 642180, 'end': 676120}, 'sentences_idx_start': 52, 'sentences_idx_end': 53}, {'text': "So what's kind of been proposed as one of the leading models of this is the relaxed belief under psychedelics model, the Rebus model of Carhartt, Harris and Tristan. And so this builds on the kind of like active inference, hierarchical predictive processing framework where we can understand the brain as this series of predictors stacked kind of like hierarchically along brain networks. And predictions are being made by higher level networks that are attempting to predict the errors of lower level networks.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8514764308929443, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.25732937455177307, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.127237007021904, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.12575550377368927, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.04457360878586769, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.020219137892127037, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.017078770324587822, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.009844310581684113, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.007746445946395397, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.002960829297080636, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 678480, 'end': 722520}, 'sentences_idx_start': 54, 'sentences_idx_end': 56}, {'text': "And the process of basically doing this then produces this series of belief landscapes at different levels of spatiotemporal abstraction. And these belief landscapes, of course, can encode beliefs with various levels of precision. And it's the modulation of the precision of these beliefs which is believed to take place under psychedelic use. So here's kind of like a very high level version of this Rebus model and how belief relaxation might actually happen, right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8435778617858887, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.5665149688720703, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.48339954018592834, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.01853063888847828, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.015485137701034546, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.009234735742211342, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.006994277238845825, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.006114664953202009, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.003648508107289672, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.003403904614970088, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 724060, 'end': 764222}, 'sentences_idx_start': 57, 'sentences_idx_end': 60}, {'text': 'So given that you have this series of cortical networks which are representing beliefs at different spatiotemporal scales. We can kind of think of the thalamus as being kind of like the entry point where sensory information is being gated into this hierarchical system and the prefrontal cortex as being kind of like one of the highest level. Networks, which is then responsible for both representing the most abstract kinds of beliefs as well as being kind of the primary inhibiting force for all of the downstream beliefs in the network, in the system.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.20070452988147736, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.16136862337589264, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.14832191169261932, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.09907381236553192, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.028783338144421577, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.015817955136299133, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.011601566337049007, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.003891546046361327, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.001814960385672748, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0014961410779505968, 'label': 'Science'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 764276, 'end': 801900}, 'sentences_idx_start': 61, 'sentences_idx_end': 63}, {'text': "So what is this heavy agonism of the five h T two A receptor supposed to be doing in this case? Well, it's going to be decreasing the prefrontal cortex's ability to make coherent predictions and coherent representations of belief, which will then disrupt its ability to inhibit lower levels of the cortical hierarchy. At the same time, by disrupt this activation of the Salamic or this disruption of the thalamic gating is going to result in additional sensory information entering the cortex that wouldn't underwise enter the cortex.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5780134201049805, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.04827491194009781, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.03670688346028328, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.03260260075330734, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.021596744656562805, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01260918378829956, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005212915129959583, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.0031882491894066334, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0012816009111702442, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0012628085678443313, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 803070, 'end': 842302}, 'sentences_idx_start': 64, 'sentences_idx_end': 66}, {'text': "You have these kind of disruptions at these two levels which then result in beliefs being spontaneously represented in ways that they wouldn't normally be represented. And the Rebus model at least is suggesting that this mainly is going to manifest itself as a kind of relaxation of these beliefs. So here is a kind of like very simple diagram of what this might look like.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7965806126594543, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.765988826751709, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.6972588300704956, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.14472435414791107, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.043923888355493546, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.003231719369068742, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.0020623174495995045, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0019177930662408471, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0019017643062397838, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0009112182888202369, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 842466, 'end': 876740}, 'sentences_idx_start': 67, 'sentences_idx_end': 69}, {'text': 'So you have some landscape of beliefs here and you can kind of interpret the position along the X and Y or, I guess, the X and Z belief in A as being corresponding to some particular belief that might be represented by the network at this layer or at this level of representation. And then the Y axis, the height as being the actual precision of that belief. Right?', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8571403622627258, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.08897914737462997, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0036200666800141335, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet'}, {'relevance': 0.0035394562873989344, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.003023975295946002, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}, {'relevance': 0.0020443168468773365, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0010489547858014703, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetForBeginners'}, {'relevance': 0.0008497984381392598, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0007582801044918597, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007471933495253325, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>HomeUtilities>InternetServiceProviders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 877270, 'end': 906958}, 'sentences_idx_start': 70, 'sentences_idx_end': 72}, {'text': "So here we have this kind of very deep part on the right part of this network or on this landscape and this would be a very strongly represented belief. Let's say what the acute effects of psychedelics are then understood to be doing right is to be flattening this landscape to be less strongly representing these strongly represented beliefs to maybe making it easier for the reversal of this landscape.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5785091519355774, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.21891161799430847, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.10855873674154282, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.04999420419335365, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.02537580393254757, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.015888987109065056, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.012238438241183758, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.003709967713803053, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0024575127754360437, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.001960113411769271, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 907124, 'end': 934034}, 'sentences_idx_start': 73, 'sentences_idx_end': 74}, {'text': 'So to move from one attractor state to another tractor state, which is meant to be understood to be kind of therapeutic in various ways, and then the post acute effect being some kind of return to normalcy, but one that is not totally complete, one that still incorporates some of these newly relaxed beliefs, these newly explored beliefs.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.13707087934017181, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.11566528677940369, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.11227038502693176, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.045505404472351074, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.012637021020054817, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01113240234553814, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0038507587742060423, 'label': 'Sports>EquineSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0036402579862624407, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.003490021452307701, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.0028607368003576994, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 934082, 'end': 958430}, 'sentences_idx_start': 75, 'sentences_idx_end': 75}, {'text': 'Building on this rebus model, karin Harris and colleagues last year proposed this canal model of psychopathology, which basically kind of takes the intuition that the relaxation, if the Reevis model is correct, if the relaxation of beliefs has a therapeutic outcome. If you kind of take that way of thinking to its logical conclusion, you might then propose something like this, which would say if relaxing overly strong beliefs therapeutic, then having overly strong beliefs in the first place is pathological in some kind of way.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8529160022735596, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.062211427837610245, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.029669465497136116, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.029467834159731865, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.026104411110281944, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.01950865611433983, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.019332299008965492, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.01627548411488533, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01332966797053814, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.008067980408668518, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 963560, 'end': 1005170}, 'sentences_idx_start': 76, 'sentences_idx_end': 77}, {'text': 'And they refer to this development of these overly strongly represented beliefs as canalized beliefs and this problem generally as canalization or this process of developing them as canalization. And this is the canal model of psych pathology. So they kind of build on this idea, this set of previous work in the literature suggesting that there may be some primary factor of psychopathology and they suggest that this primary factor is canalization. And in this work they discuss a number of different psychopathologies which seem to quite clearly fit this canalization type characterization.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8219285011291504, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.3514711260795593, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.25272876024246216, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.11707132309675217, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.06792307645082474, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.0564553402364254, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.04370160400867462, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.02603660337626934, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.014793181791901588, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.007038369309157133, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1006580, 'end': 1051020}, 'sentences_idx_start': 78, 'sentences_idx_end': 81}, {'text': "So it's very relatively straightforward I think, to understand things like addiction, depression, anxiety disorders, obsessive compulsive disorders. All of these involve in one way or another having some strongly held beliefs, typically negative, negative beliefs in the case of like, depression, anxiety, obsessive compulsive, body image disorder, or in the case of substance use disorder, some very strong beliefs about what kind of behaviors should be taken at any given time in any given context.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9807425737380981, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.5655063390731812, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.017281314358115196, 'label': "HealthyLiving>Men'sHealth"}, {'relevance': 0.007682429160922766, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005025305785238743, 'label': 'HealthyLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.0039250971749424934, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0031610873993486166, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>SmokingCessation'}, {'relevance': 0.0021252937149256468, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.001723029650747776, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.001460366416722536, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingTeens'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1051180, 'end': 1085180}, 'sentences_idx_start': 82, 'sentences_idx_end': 83}, {'text': "And then of course, the effect of psychedelics is to undo canalization and the better able any sort of therapeutic intervention is to undo canalization, the more likely for a positive therapeutic outcome. So I think this work has a lot of strengths and there's a kind of elegance to it.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.29370421171188354, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.1469402313232422, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.11377864331007004, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.022022631019353867, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00998744461685419, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.009486479684710503, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.006489323917776346, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0039786724373698235, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.003709398675709963, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0028331144712865353, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1087440, 'end': 1110230}, 'sentences_idx_start': 84, 'sentences_idx_end': 85}, {'text': "In our deep Pinal's work that we've worked on, we kind of identify a couple of limitations of this canal model and attempt to extend and refine the model in ways that I think ultimately make it more powerful, while kind of keeping the essential elegant insight that cannibalization is kind of like intimately tied to pathology. So the first kind of limitation I think that we identify is that in the canal model it's very heavily implied that all forms of canalization are pathological in one way or another.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.16538678109645844, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>DigestiveDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.09734491258859634, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.07828395813703537, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.04402239993214607, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Cancer'}, {'relevance': 0.02893143892288208, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>Surgery'}, {'relevance': 0.018133390694856644, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Ear,NoseAndThroatConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0045571476221084595, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.003944662865251303, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.0033292861189693213, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>InfectiousDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.0023486933205276728, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>CosmeticMedicalServices'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1111800, 'end': 1155250}, 'sentences_idx_start': 86, 'sentences_idx_end': 87}, {'text': "And as I mentioned just now, this is clearly the case for a large class of very common psychopathologies. It's when we start to look more towards edge cases, I think that these exceptions start to problematize this understanding, right? So if we consider psychopathologies such as bipolar, borderline schizophrenia, depersonalization disorder, it becomes much more difficult to kind of easily classify these as simply problems of overly strong priors.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9919852018356323, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.581869900226593, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.11144198477268219, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.021975887939333916, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01470133289694786, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.0035357936285436153, 'label': "HealthyLiving>Men'sHealth"}, {'relevance': 0.0025197290815413, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.0018337649526074529, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0015682352241128683, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0011765861418098211, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1155620, 'end': 1190540}, 'sentences_idx_start': 88, 'sentences_idx_end': 90}, {'text': 'In many cases here we have problems of priors that are not so strong or priors that seem to drift over time in ways that are problematic for both the individual and the people that the individual are close to. And if we think about psychedelics then as being this kind of panacea to undo cannibalization and undo psychopathology, we also run into this other issue which is that there are certain kinds of psychopathologies which are typically issues for use with psychedelics, right?', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.173334538936615, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.10042522847652435, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.02942945621907711, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.00978891272097826, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships'}, {'relevance': 0.0097527289763093, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0053003584034740925, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0051990412175655365, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0035267164930701256, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting'}, {'relevance': 0.0033256520982831717, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0030861308332532644, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1190880, 'end': 1229016}, 'sentences_idx_start': 91, 'sentences_idx_end': 92}, {'text': "So schizophrenia being a very clear one, where there's evidence of psychedelic use being a trigger for the onset of psychosis in individuals who are predisposed to schizophrenia. There's also evidence of the development of depersonalization disorders with strong psychedelic use. And this is not what we would expect if psychedelics were simply universally undoing or getting rid of psychopathologies.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7108561992645264, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.15017707645893097, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.05635391175746918, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.030442362651228905, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.005070441402494907, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0036765781696885824, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0033362172544002533, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0030129875522106886, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0013111475855112076, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0007112869643606246, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1229038, 'end': 1259620}, 'sentences_idx_start': 93, 'sentences_idx_end': 95}, {'text': "There's also this idea, which I think Adam is going to develop quite a bit later, that the stability of beliefs is typically correlated with positive mental health outcomes, not negative ones. And what is a stable belief if not one that is highly analyzed in some kind of meaningful sense within the system?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9733672142028809, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.41451629996299744, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.06364309042692184, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.04666569456458092, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.027791285887360573, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.018175294622778893, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.008160527795553207, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.006141956429928541, 'label': 'HealthyLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.003828455461189151, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0033170951064676046, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1260760, 'end': 1281210}, 'sentences_idx_start': 96, 'sentences_idx_end': 97}, {'text': "And a second limitation is that if you think about an actual dynamical system, one that is parameterized in some kind of meaningful way, like a brain, which is parameterized by synaptic connections and then instantiates neural activity patterns over time, and we think about what kinds of optimization landscapes are actually being induced by such a system. We find that there's not just one kind of canalization, there's actually two kinds of canalization.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.24732470512390137, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.013827495276927948, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.010437656193971634, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.003928469028323889, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.002670779824256897, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0017966945888474584, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.001685646129772067, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0012303412659093738, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0009685552795417607, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>MechanicalAndIndustrialEngineeringIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.000752801017370075, 'label': 'Science'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1286240, 'end': 1322280}, 'sentences_idx_start': 98, 'sentences_idx_end': 99}, {'text': "And in our deep canals work, we attempt to kind of take inspiration from deep learning literature to tease apart these two kinds of canalization and understand them a bit more clearly. And they are just to kind of give a preview these two different things, overfitting and plasticity loss. So overfitting is the problem of your canalized in a particular kind of way and whatever sort of policy you've learned, whatever sort of set of beliefs you have, these don't generalize to some other context.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2282334268093109, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.01661054790019989, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0035458309575915337, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007412896957248449, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007279806886799634, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0005470593459904194, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.000485579832457006, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0004077510966453701, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0003985961084254086, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0003950897662434727, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1324060, 'end': 1361984}, 'sentences_idx_start': 100, 'sentences_idx_end': 102}, {'text': "You're in context A, you may be very well adapted, you move to context B and whatever you've learned doesn't apply there, then plasticity loss is a little bit different. Plasticity loss has to do with not one's ability to generalize, but rather one's ability to adapt or to learn. So imagine you're in context A, you may or may not be well adapted to context A.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.004578430205583572, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.004080887418240309, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.002476536901667714, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0023511191830039024, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.0015171105042099953, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0014966190792620182, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BoneAndJointConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0010638675885275006, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0007168357260525227, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0005949033657088876, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>FootHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0005687566590495408, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1362112, 'end': 1388508}, 'sentences_idx_start': 103, 'sentences_idx_end': 105}, {'text': 'If you move to context B, the question becomes are you able to adapt to context B or not? Not. Are you immediately already ready to deal with context B? But given time in context B, can you learn and change? And we use a very simple recurrent neural network model to kind of make sense of this. And I think this is important because there can be different kinds of canalization on these different kinds of optimization landscapes and these have unique implications for the treatment of psychopathology.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8918226957321167, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.08633972704410553, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.01385257113724947, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.012714768759906292, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01093325950205326, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.004293861333280802, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.003333805128931999, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.002322516171261668, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0019354441901668906, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0019038645550608635, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1388594, 'end': 1427080}, 'sentences_idx_start': 106, 'sentences_idx_end': 111}, {'text': "And I think even more importantly, psychedelics work on these different landscapes in different ways. And so understanding how they work is essential to developing better drugs, better treatment protocols and more personalized treatment. Okay, so what are these two optimization landscapes? How can we make sense of them? This is kind of like the big overview figure of the deep canal's work. So we kind of start with this intuition of a recurrent neural network, right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7556422352790833, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.043438415974378586, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.013622944243252277, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.005337683018296957, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.004673260264098644, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>PharmaceuticalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0031877777073532343, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.003021874465048313, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0027982951141893864, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002082294784486294, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.002044438384473324, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1427500, 'end': 1464436}, 'sentences_idx_start': 112, 'sentences_idx_end': 117}, {'text': "And in a recurrent neural network there are these two sets of parameters that you have at any given time. You have the actual weights of the network and then you have the hidden activation of the network, right? And so the weights of the network are theta and the hidden activation is h and there's some input into the network at any given time step. And then the output of the network is a function of both the input and the hidden state.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04300457984209061, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0019401883473619819, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0008611258235760033, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0006930966046638787, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003626576217357069, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00018337828805670142, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0001775596319930628, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0001709333882899955, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0001653511862969026, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.000160887255333364, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1464458, 'end': 1491628}, 'sentences_idx_start': 118, 'sentences_idx_end': 121}, {'text': 'And the hidden state is updated at every time the hidden activation pattern. And this gives us essentially these two different landscapes. One, what we refer to as the inference landscape or the type A landscape. And this is equivalent to the neural activation pattern of a brain at any time.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.003241500351577997, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0030859753023833036, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0025156012270599604, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0021500620059669018, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.002004537731409073, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0019518102053552866, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00194736965931952, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.001670507830567658, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.001586006605066359, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.001585246529430151, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1491794, 'end': 1509108}, 'sentences_idx_start': 122, 'sentences_idx_end': 125}, {'text': 'So what gets read off from an fMRI, what gets read off from the EEG is going to correspond to this activity landscape, but kind of like underlying or supporting this activity landscape is this other more fundamental landscape which is the actual optimization landscape that is induced by the synaptic weights themselves. And this is what is the result of right click synaptic connectivity in the brain between all the sets of neurons in the brain. This is what is changing when we have various forms of heavy and plasticity heavy in learning.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.03188934177160263, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.016488779336214066, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.010854426771402359, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.008272571489214897, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.007879572920501232, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>ExerciseAndFitnessVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.006689462810754776, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0037865114863961935, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0021061482839286327, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.001946827513165772, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.001401806017383933, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1509194, 'end': 1545390}, 'sentences_idx_start': 126, 'sentences_idx_end': 128}, {'text': "And this is what kind of instantiates the possible sets of neural activity patterns, right? So this is kind of like a way we can start to understand this, which is when we think about belief landscapes, right? As I mentioned before, here's a very simple diagram where we have a two dimensional belief landscape. And let's say there's someone who's depressed or potentially depressed and they might have a negative self image. I'm a terrible person, I can't do anything right.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.1425456404685974, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.11284437775611877, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.04270961880683899, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0346730537712574, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.025221098214387894, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.021211519837379456, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.020028984174132347, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.018158122897148132, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01786065474152565, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004334781318902969, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1547840, 'end': 1584152}, 'sentences_idx_start': 129, 'sentences_idx_end': 133}, {'text': "Something like this. This would be encoded as a particular position in this belief landscape. When the neural activity pattern looks like this, this belief is what gets expressed, right? And there's another set of neural activity patterns which would correspond to a positive self image, a positive self belief, I'm great, I'm wonderful, or even just, I'm okay, I'm totally acceptable as a person. And this would be a different set of patterns.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.11973503977060318, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.04884093999862671, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.02532188966870308, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.01447900291532278, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.009397107176482677, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.005220511928200722, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.004913013428449631, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004910270683467388, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.003100153524428606, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.0030310105066746473, 'label': "HealthyLiving>Men'sHealth"}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1584206, 'end': 1613060}, 'sentences_idx_start': 134, 'sentences_idx_end': 138}, {'text': 'So based on the synaptic, the actual connectivity structure of the brain, these two patterns may be more or less likely. So here these are being represented by these two different sets of neural activation landscapes which are the result of two different positions in this synaptic weight landscape space.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5769254565238953, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.011237772181630135, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.010473241098225117, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0017572306096553802, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.001223812927491963, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0010308100609108806, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Injuries'}, {'relevance': 0.0007443370996043086, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0005677776644006371, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0004909044364467263, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0004053925222251564, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1614200, 'end': 1636830}, 'sentences_idx_start': 139, 'sentences_idx_end': 140}, {'text': "And in this top space, the one that's in the middle of here that then is represented here at the top of part C of the figure, we see that there's very high precision assigned to or very high likelihood assigned to the negative self image and very low likelihood here assigned to the positive self image. But in some other part of the synaptic weight landscape, a very different kind of neural activity landscape might be instantiated.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.754344642162323, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.013003667816519737, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.012837477028369904, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.006305748131126165, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0029128319583833218, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0025838431902229786, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0023478420916944742, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0021233935840427876, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0010344735346734524, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.000988029525615275, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1637200, 'end': 1672612}, 'sentences_idx_start': 141, 'sentences_idx_end': 142}, {'text': 'And this one kind of has the inverse properties where negative self image is unlikely and positive self image is much more likely. So we can kind of then understand positions in the neural activity landscape as kind of corresponding to specific phenomenological experiential instantiations of certain kinds of beliefs, right? So like the actual experience of holding a negative self image or holding a positive self image. And we can understand positions in the synaptic weight landscape as being something more general.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.07309520244598389, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.027048131451010704, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.02511020191013813, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.022547170519828796, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01598758064210415, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.013073829934000969, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0046288021840155125, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.004389261826872826, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.002194657688960433, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.0018724254332482815, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1672756, 'end': 1708500}, 'sentences_idx_start': 143, 'sentences_idx_end': 146}, {'text': "So in the case of depression, there might be a specific set of synaptic weight connectivity which would correspond to what you might call a depressed individual, someone who might qualify as having major depressive disorder and another set of synaptic weights connectivity pattern that wouldn't qualify as that. Okay, so before I get into the psychedelic, how psychedelics relate to this, I think Adam is going to talk a little bit about some work he's done extending the hello.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5072964429855347, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.3144145607948303, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.13116423785686493, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0038643565494567156, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.002978953067213297, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0021605787333101034, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0010036081075668335, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.0006952188559807837, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0006860272260382771, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0005957354442216456, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1708570, 'end': 1762160}, 'sentences_idx_start': 147, 'sentences_idx_end': 148}, {'text': "So, yeah, I've been thinking about this a while and then along the way I met Arthur, who also has been thinking about this a while, but in different ways. And so like Arthur's background is in basically consciousness science and a very peculiar field of computational consciousness science in terms of actual models of what it would be to have a conscious system, even potentially an artificially conscious system.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9467570185661316, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.022661177441477776, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.011111339554190636, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.005707316566258669, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0030149207450449467, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0013929575216025114, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.001319287228398025, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Sci-fiAndFantasy'}, {'relevance': 0.0005934275104664266, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00044797471491619945, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0004367176443338394, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1763570, 'end': 1796166}, 'sentences_idx_start': 149, 'sentences_idx_end': 150}, {'text': "And so I'm coming from more free energy principle and active inference, my background and Arthur's coming from more mainstream machine learning. And so we were coming together to explore this beast from different perspectives and been finding a lot of, I think, very interesting overlap. And so in terms of Albus, the basic idea is to take Rebus and expand on it. I love rebus.", 'la