 something else, another belief, and that strengthening it could be a good thing.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7313428521156311, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.4376448392868042, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.16620053350925446, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.13646434247493744, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.008308930322527885, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0044212485663592815, 'label': 'HealthyLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.003879610449075699, 'label': 'Careers>CareerPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.003245119471102953, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0028861237224191427, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.002086430788040161, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2215090, 'end': 2229314}, 'sentences_idx_start': 202, 'sentences_idx_end': 204}, {'text': "And even without a clinical context, like microdosers, for instance, it's not clear exactly they're trying to relax their beliefs, like the range of use cases, the way we want to relate them and how we want to be in the world. It seems complicated to me. So I will take it back to Arthur. Great. Yeah. Thanks so much, Adam.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9960934519767761, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.9938936829566956, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.29085949063301086, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.11598845571279526, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>PharmaceuticalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.052271127700805664, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.003124573500826955, 'label': 'HealthyLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.0028239714447408915, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.0026771188713610172, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>SmokingCessation'}, {'relevance': 0.0022969061974436045, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.002010586205869913, 'label': 'MedicalHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2229352, 'end': 2259980}, 'sentences_idx_start': 205, 'sentences_idx_end': 210}, {'text': 'OK, so with that context of Alice, I want to talk a little bit about how we might understand at a very high level what psychedelics are doing to these two belief landscapes. So before I showed you very quickly, I guess I can go back to it.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9734131693840027, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.8532870411872864, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.5844787359237671, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.025770269334316254, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.019698701798915863, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.014073251746594906, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.011048074811697006, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0085384426638484, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.006702316924929619, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.004367077257484198, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2261040, 'end': 2278710}, 'sentences_idx_start': 211, 'sentences_idx_end': 212}, {'text': "In the Rebus model there's only one type of optimization landscape and so there's only one type of canalization and what is supposed to be happening is a relaxation of leaves which is strong during the acute effect and persists in the post acute effect. So with albus though, we might be able to think about all of this a little bit differently.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.006107933819293976, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.0043753450736403465, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.002833553357049823, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0016431143740192056, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.0009575206786394119, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0009034471586346626, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.0009009465575218201, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0008766609244048595, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>PharmaceuticalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0008425150299444795, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0006490690866485238, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2279240, 'end': 2303020}, 'sentences_idx_start': 213, 'sentences_idx_end': 214}, {'text': "We can, enduring the acute effects of psychedelics, interpret what's happening to the type A landscape as being less of a kind of universal relaxation and more of a kind of destabilization where under certain circumstances beliefs are being strengthened, other beliefs. Are being relaxed. This is changing quite rapidly over the course of time. So a certain belief might be transiently strengthened a few minutes later, it may no longer be supported or supportable.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5494998097419739, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.20343077182769775, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.03270766884088516, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.027981869876384735, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.026104070246219635, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.01877759024500847, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01257211435586214, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.011595591902732849, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.003706004237756133, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.0035899896174669266, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2304160, 'end': 2335800}, 'sentences_idx_start': 215, 'sentences_idx_end': 218}, {'text': 'And this actually functionally enables a kind of exploration of a wide space of belief instantiations during the acute effects of the drug. As far as the inference landscape is concerned, post acute effects, as Adam was saying, it could be the fact that certain positive beliefs are explored and can be strengthened, other negative beliefs might be weakened. This is kind of like the ideal psychotherapeutic outcome. It may be on average that something like a relaxation, a general relaxation of beliefs is what you might see.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.16519348323345184, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.10364194959402084, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.05729420855641365, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.045101940631866455, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.04168868064880371, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.03592026233673096, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.008394687436521053, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.005803195293992758, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.004810421261936426, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.004383683204650879, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2337900, 'end': 2376692}, 'sentences_idx_start': 219, 'sentences_idx_end': 222}, {'text': "But the way that you get there is likely going to be through a kind of much more complicated process, I think. What's then interesting and related also to what Adam said about thinking much more broadly about how psychedelics might be used in terms of neurocognitive disorders, in addition to kind of like traditional psychopathologies is to think about what's happening to the learning landscape, the kind of like underlying synaptic weight landscape.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.4593442976474762, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.05113569647073746, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.04689450189471245, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.037556279450654984, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.022180886939167976, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.012401684187352657, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.011434320360422134, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.007172327488660812, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.004236784763634205, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.003130657132714987, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2376826, 'end': 2404024}, 'sentences_idx_start': 223, 'sentences_idx_end': 224}, {'text': "And what do we understand is happening here kind of quite clearly is there is neurogenesis psychoplastogenic effects, there's dendritic growth. And what is this enabling? Well, this is enabling greater connectivity between, within and between networks. And so kind of from a functional learning perspective, learning theory perspective, what this means is that gradient information can flow more easily through these networks. And what this means is that it's easier to get from one part of the network to the other part of the network.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3787461817264557, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.007045591715723276, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.003941460512578487, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.003336857771500945, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.002734009874984622, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.001237584394402802, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0007954573375172913, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0005613083485513926, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0003769268514588475, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Injuries'}, {'relevance': 0.0003569398249965161, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingTeens'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2404152, 'end': 2440708}, 'sentences_idx_start': 225, 'sentences_idx_end': 229}, {'text': 'There are fewer of these kind of optimization local minima, there are fewer of these kind of tricky saddle points. And what this means kind of like functionally is that this plasticity loss that I discussed earlier is going to be less of an issue. And here it seems to be kind of like regardless of the acute, the actual phenomenological effects, there are very strong downstream effects on this structural connectivity.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.026620743796229362, 'label': 'Sports>EquineSports'}, {'relevance': 0.00353166158311069, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>ReproductiveHealth>Pregnancy'}, {'relevance': 0.002349564805626869, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BoneAndJointConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0006956132128834724, 'label': 'Sports>EquineSports>HorseRacing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005038873641751707, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise>RunningAndJogging'}, {'relevance': 0.00042861822294071317, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>FootHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0003967258962802589, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0002506188757251948, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.00024256817414425313, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00021514172840397805, 'label': 'Pets>VeterinaryMedicine'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2440804, 'end': 2472832}, 'sentences_idx_start': 230, 'sentences_idx_end': 232}, {'text': "And I think there's some interesting work suggesting that there may actually be independent mechanisms that are affecting these two landscapes. So there's recent work suggesting for example that psychedelics as well as ketamine is able to kind of particularly bind to receptors in the brain that produce that result in the kind of release of the brain derived neurotrophic factor and then the downstream changes in synaptic weighting and that this may be potentially totally independent of the five H C two a agonism. Right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.13075914978981018, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.04969621077179909, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.04203552380204201, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.009114416316151619, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0011170369107276201, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0010993503965437412, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.000762437004595995, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0007099189679138362, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.0006576828309334815, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0005571318906731904, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2472976, 'end': 2508290}, 'sentences_idx_start': 233, 'sentences_idx_end': 235}, {'text': "And this has very interesting implications for future drug design and development. Okay, so I'm going to, before my next slide, turn it over to Adam once more to briefly talk a bit about personality theory and the relationship between psychedelics and hello again.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7306850552558899, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.19354590773582458, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.04703385382890701, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.03588588163256645, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.029691563919186592, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.013945865444839, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>PharmaceuticalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0032875328324735165, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0026540979743003845, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0021841416601091623, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>SmokingCessation'}, {'relevance': 0.001954336417838931, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2510420, 'end': 2533160}, 'sentences_idx_start': 236, 'sentences_idx_end': 237}, {'text': "So for the past few years I've been doing some work with a personality researcher, Colin de Jung, on intersections between the way agency is modeled in the free energy principle and active inference framework and the way that persons are considered in different situations in personality science and looking for points of intersection. Personality is actually an extremely deep concept.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.07931143045425415, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.05650223419070244, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.03244633600115776, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.02045241743326187, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.015239624306559563, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.00926502700895071, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.008407601155340672, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.006222657393664122, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.005400083027780056, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.004489652346819639, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2537290, 'end': 2565066}, 'sentences_idx_start': 238, 'sentences_idx_end': 239}, {'text': "And if you think of it, I guess we call it like the normal form of a system in terms of what is the way you can describe the most of the system with like the minimal message length, the account for the most of the least. And what we're trying to account for is the states that people tend to occupy, people aren't always happy, people aren't always sad, people aren't always friendly, they're not always angry.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2092287838459015, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Email'}, {'relevance': 0.10686718672513962, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.01677573472261429, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.007324133068323135, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.005868762265890837, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.003690935904160142, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002730842214077711, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.0017833817983046174, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.0017477981746196747, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}, {'relevance': 0.0016910769045352936, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2565098, 'end': 2591826}, 'sentences_idx_start': 240, 'sentences_idx_end': 241}, {'text': "It's all sorts of things that there's a range that people are encountering but they tend to occupy some states more than others. And you might call that their personality and you might call it many systems would have their own personalities in terms of trying to describe something like their essence and so they're attracting states.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3569701313972473, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.07143475860357285, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.04228419438004494, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.008402140811085701, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.005040609743446112, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0038770127575844526, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.002616769867017865, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0019524204544723034, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0014815672766417265, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.0011413819156587124, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2591858, 'end': 2610320}, 'sentences_idx_start': 242, 'sentences_idx_end': 243}, {'text': "And so with Colin de Jung's work, he interprets personality and these major domains of personality that people have discovered a reliable factor structure ways you can chunk the variance, the big five as a trait hierarchy but where these different traits are interpreted as cybernetic control parameters. Specifically cybernetics in terms of the study of goal seeking systems governed by various forms of feedback that different stages of the process of pursuing goals, evaluating outcomes updating understanding that basically the personality as different modes of being in the world.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.894986093044281, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.08061086386442184, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.01799582690000534, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.009792860597372055, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.008564259856939316, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.005567931570112705, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.005453283898532391, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004924919456243515, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.0039075748063623905, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.002907304558902979, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2610850, 'end': 2654394}, 'sentences_idx_start': 244, 'sentences_idx_end': 245}, {'text': "For cybernetic systems, interpreting them as parameters for goal pursuit because we are goal seeking systems trying to pursue the goals we value. And so I guess moving to this with relation to what we're talking about now, both in terms of personality formation, reformation and the structure of personality, to get to the P factor within personality theory, this big five traits, the set of big five traits, there's a richer or more detailed factor structure, a hierarchical structure for personality that's been discovered.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9965935349464417, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.7352748513221741, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.009299525059759617, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00821223296225071, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.006211991887539625, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0019347231136634946, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0014429448638111353, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0014350565616041422, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Off-RoadVehicles'}, {'relevance': 0.001325925113633275, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0011939905816689134, 'label': 'Careers>CareerPlanning'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2654432, 'end': 2696710}, 'sentences_idx_start': 246, 'sentences_idx_end': 247}, {'text': "So above the Big Five, neuroticism, agreeableness, conscientiousness, you'll have a metatrate of their shared various that's observed called stability. It's also been called alpha by, I think, Digman. And then above the traits of extroversion and openness intellect, you have this MetaTrade of plasticity and are called beta and the shared variants of these two.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.09145641326904297, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.013734360225498676, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.011562583968043327, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.008393754251301289, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004765856545418501, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.002726792125031352, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.002144986530765891, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0020489466842263937, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingTeens'}, {'relevance': 0.0018425540765747428, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0018240936333313584, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2696870, 'end': 2722900}, 'sentences_idx_start': 248, 'sentences_idx_end': 250}, {'text': "So what's interesting is that within this field of within high top, which is this effort to try to characterize psychopathology using the same kind of data driven methods in personality science. A principled account of the structure of psychopathology, the way that personality has a structure and trying to account for this, there seems to be a common factor across many forms of psychopathology that's referred to as the P factor and it tends to be the inverse of stability. It's high neuroticism, low agreeableness and low conscientiousness.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7761512994766235, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.019437862560153008, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.005937811452895403, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.004881755914539099, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0036754498723894358, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0031540500931441784, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0028382339514791965, 'label': "HealthyLiving>Men'sHealth"}, {'relevance': 0.002331963274627924, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0021964984480291605, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.002181196352466941, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2723270, 'end': 2760634}, 'sentences_idx_start': 251, 'sentences_idx_end': 253}, {'text': "And this is actually what's referred to in the article as this P factor, thinking of it as a lack of flexibility. You could make a case for it. But more straightforwardly it seems to be a lack of stability. For something to be a lack of flexibility you would maybe be thinking of something more like plasticity, like someone having low plasticity. But empirically that's not what's observed.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.16111820936203003, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BoneAndJointConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0008183381869457662, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Injuries'}, {'relevance': 0.000678963609971106, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.000631185423117131, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>FootHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0005794755998067558, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}, {'relevance': 0.00047325508785434067, 'label': 'Sports>EquineSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0003007023478858173, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Microcar'}, {'relevance': 0.00028342471341602504, 'label': 'Science>Geology'}, {'relevance': 0.0002558726991992444, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.00024446274619549513, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2760762, 'end': 2789938}, 'sentences_idx_start': 254, 'sentences_idx_end': 258}, {'text': "And so if empirically that's not what's observed, that's a very important detail we should stop and take note of. So you might say that rather than emphasizing the first principal component of psychopathology, it's possible that this Canal model is actually focusing on the second factor. It's not a contest. It's still enormously a big factor like the work of Stephen Hayes and others showing that a lack of flexibility is transdiagnostic.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9834729433059692, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.2742774486541748, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.029570354148745537, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.011316074058413506, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004422222264111042, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.003270524088293314, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.0020231464877724648, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0017193494131788611, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.00123006128706038, 'label': 'HealthyLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.001144029782153666, 'label': "HealthyLiving>Men'sHealth"}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2790034, 'end': 2818202}, 'sentences_idx_start': 259, 'sentences_idx_end': 262}, {'text': "But just empirically speaking, the first principal component of psychopathology might be more closely related to a lack of stability rather than insufficient plasticity. I guess one more thing to think of in terms of stability and like as it's not exactly a contest, they're both important, both need to be considered and they're deeply interrelated. So Colin describes them as being in a state of something like dynamic tension.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9092956781387329, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.11046208441257477, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.014582530595362186, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.009374726563692093, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.004843809176236391, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0036910497583448887, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0018274392932653427, 'label': "HealthyLiving>Men'sHealth"}, {'relevance': 0.0011725281365215778, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0011072773486375809, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0010430853581055999, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2818346, 'end': 2849654}, 'sentences_idx_start': 263, 'sentences_idx_end': 265}, {'text': "Like if you're insufficiently plastic and inflexible, you're not going to stay stable for long in a changing world, but if you don't have a stable base to move from, it's going to be hard to be plastic and reconfigure yourself in a sustainable way either. However, you could also see someone being overly rigid and excessive stability in a way that undermines their plasticity or overly flexible in a way that basically is destabilizing. So a dynamic tension but involving synergies also.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8991873860359192, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>GreenSolutions'}, {'relevance': 0.3072144389152527, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EnvironmentalServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.12964366376399994, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.0028523385990411043, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>PowerAndEnergyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.002283309353515506, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy'}, {'relevance': 0.0022826457861810923, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0022142468951642513, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>ApparelIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.002094428287819028, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>GreenVehicles'}, {'relevance': 0.0018652866128832102, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FrugalLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.0016458325553685427, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2849782, 'end': 2879698}, 'sentences_idx_start': 266, 'sentences_idx_end': 268}, {'text': "And I think in terms of the structure of personality and well being, this is what we need to keep in mind that both are needed, stability and plasticity. And this is also just within it's actually what this was inspired, I think in Colin's thinking to consider these metatrades this way from machine learning, I think actually reading Grossberg and Stability plasticity trade offs and that's why he interpreted these metatrades in those terms.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9747597575187683, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.002690445864573121, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0023490653838962317, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0022954270243644714, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.0022644242271780968, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.001671654754318297, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>HumanResources'}, {'relevance': 0.001617663772776723, 'label': 'Careers>CareerPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0015733690233901143, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0013145911507308483, 'label': 'Careers>JobSearch'}, {'relevance': 0.0012788543244823813, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2879864, 'end': 2906060}, 'sentences_idx_start': 269, 'sentences_idx_end': 270}, {'text': "So I guess one more thing is there is a Petersonian backstory here that I don't know if I want to get into, but we can discuss it later if there's yeah, back to Arthur. That was great. Thanks. Adams yeah, very, very helpful context which should hopefully make this slide here much more clear to everyone.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.02573186531662941, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Biographies'}, {'relevance': 0.005703205242753029, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature'}, {'relevance': 0.004694030154496431, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Fiction'}, {'relevance': 0.0037926791701465845, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>Screenwriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0024766982533037663, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0013126919511705637, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.0011176563566550612, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>ComicsAndGraphicNovels'}, {'relevance': 0.0010400657774880528, 'label': 'Movies>FantasyMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.0009681686060503125, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>RoleplayingGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0005693071871064603, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Sci-fiAndFantasy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2906990, 'end': 2937470}, 'sentences_idx_start': 271, 'sentences_idx_end': 274}, {'text': "So given these kind of, like, two meta traits, stability and plasticity, which, as Adam beautifully described you're in this kind of dynamic tension with one another, we can kind of go back to these two optimization landscapes and these machine learning concepts that I discussed earlier and couldn't try to understand how these things might all relate and ultimately relate to psychopathology. So I had hinted before that there were these kind of two types of cannibalization. We might say one being overfitting and another being plasticity loss.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8801867961883545, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.016887294128537178, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.006694486830383539, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.00421485910192132, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.002026187488809228, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0017577842809259892, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0017027466092258692, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0016378079308196902, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0015570793766528368, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0013431182596832514, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2940000, 'end': 2975780}, 'sentences_idx_start': 275, 'sentences_idx_end': 277}, {'text': 'And we can interpret these as kind of like being extremes, the kind of like canalized end of how these two optimization landscapes might manifest. So in the type A inference landscape, this looks like overfitting on one end, heavy canalization and underfitting on the other end in the machine learning context, right?', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.004081910476088524, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.003041816409677267, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0020275753922760487, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0016769447829574347, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0004447482351679355, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0004256154934410006, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003338699461892247, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0002069245820166543, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.00012751357280649245, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.00011288603855064139, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2975860, 'end': 2995148}, 'sentences_idx_start': 278, 'sentences_idx_end': 279}, {'text': 'So overfitting being having very strong rigid beliefs that are in a particular environmental context, adaptive, but are very unlikely to be adapted in any other context, underfitting being having a set of beliefs which are not adapted to the current context and also unlikely to be adapted to any other context. As far as stability is concerned, I think we can understand stability, this MetaTrade, as kind of representing the balance of these two things, right?', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.601926326751709, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.05174453184008598, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EnvironmentalServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.024294555187225342, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.018373718485236168, 'label': 'Travel>TravelLocations>PolarTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0028535746969282627, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0021208771504461765, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy'}, {'relevance': 0.0016863300697878003, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.0011738077737390995, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>GreenSolutions'}, {'relevance': 0.001089266617782414, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0010501551441848278, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2995234, 'end': 3027016}, 'sentences_idx_start': 280, 'sentences_idx_end': 281}, {'text': "You have high stability when you are either overfit to a particular context or underfit. So this means you're well fit to this context that you're in now and you're also likely to be well fit to other future contacts. I think this is also in complexity science, sometimes described as metastability, right? So you're at a stable point that will also likely be able to take you to other stable points in the future.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.12021351605653763, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.012763687409460545, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.005562094040215015, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.003010496264323592, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0019992885645478964, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0010716369142755866, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.000308593618683517, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessBanking&Finance>MergersAndAcquisitions'}, {'relevance': 0.00022829741647001356, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00018531848036218435, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.00014871718303766102, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3027118, 'end': 3052770}, 'sentences_idx_start': 282, 'sentences_idx_end': 285}, {'text': "And this kind of like ability to stay stable over time is then stability MetaTrade. We can then look at the type B, the learning landscape, where the kind of extreme version of canalization is this plasticity loss where it's very difficult to adapt to new contexts. The inverse of this is then catastrophic forgetting, where the problem is not one of adapting to new contexts, the problem is one of meaningfully retaining adaptive strategies and beliefs from previous contexts. And so obviously neither of these are desirable.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.004946061410009861, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.00429420405998826, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.0030476637184619904, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0020648608915507793, 'label': 'Education>AdultEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0014183004386723042, 'label': 'Education'}, {'relevance': 0.0008892585174180567, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0008341625216417015, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.000730031868442893, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.000626488181296736, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.00042750814463943243, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3053300, 'end': 3090220}, 'sentences_idx_start': 286, 'sentences_idx_end': 289}, {'text': 'What is desirable is some kind of balance between these two or one is able to adapt just enough to new context without forgetting previously learned things. But here the relationship to the Mediterranean plasticity is a bit different than stability, right? So as is being represented on this graph, the more plastic you are, basically the less canalized you are in the space, the more easy it is to move around. But actually extreme versions of this end up manifesting as catastrophic forgetting, at least in the machine learning context.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.936154305934906, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0033980505540966988, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0013462745118886232, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0013085253303870559, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.001133120502345264, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.000492046819999814, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00028413167456164956, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Off-RoadVehicles'}, {'relevance': 0.00018445942259859294, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.00018398111569695175, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00018080900190398097, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3092480, 'end': 3125480}, 'sentences_idx_start': 290, 'sentences_idx_end': 293}, {'text': 'And I think this in particular has relevance for psychopathology and relevance for this idea, maybe complicates this idea, right, that psychedelic therapy is in and of itself likely to always lead to positive outcomes. Okay? And we can attempt to understand this by making an effort at trying to map or understand various forms of psychology in the context of these two different learning landscapes.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9584634304046631, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.4486156404018402, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.11408405750989914, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.03056415542960167, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.02060178481042385, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.01624852605164051, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.013287891633808613, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.00462038628757, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004030197858810425, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0026180059649050236, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3125820, 'end': 3166000}, 'sentences_idx_start': 294, 'sentences_idx_end': 296}, {'text': "And so before I get into this too much, I think it's important to say that this is very much a kind of like preliminary and provisional attempt at making sense of these things. I hope that this is kind of the start of a much more fleshed out dialogue looking at how we can kind of understand psychopathology with respect to machine learning concepts.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9990785121917725, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.012346433475613594, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.006880554370582104, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.005285100545734167, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0052194297313690186, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0042578973807394505, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0030804749112576246, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.002327066147699952, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.001576502458192408, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0012722373940050602, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3166340, 'end': 3187396}, 'sentences_idx_start': 297, 'sentences_idx_end': 298}, {'text': "But I think this at least gives a good starting point for maybe trying to understand where and why psychedelic therapy is useful, isn't useful, which is a bit more nuanced than this simple idea of like psychopathology means cannibalization and psychedelic therapy means reducing cannibalization. Right? Okay, so let's try to make sense of this a little bit. So for the kind of classic set of psychopathologies for which there has been a lot of great research done with psychedelic therapy and a lot of clear benefit has been seen.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7195594310760498, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.5432940125465393, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.21035319566726685, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.014551023952662945, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.01059833262115717, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.006210667546838522, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.004668019711971283, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.003975650295615196, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00299597205594182, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0009378273971378803, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SexualHealth>SexualConditions'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3187588, 'end': 3225590}, 'sentences_idx_start': 299, 'sentences_idx_end': 302}, {'text': 'I think we can kind of class these within this upper left hand corner here, where these are disorders of both overfitting, which means in the moment overly strong beliefs get represented. These are strong attractor points in the neural activation landscape and plasticity loss in the type B landscape.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.17562589049339294, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.07425075024366379, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.014189871959388256, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.009583872742950916, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.009483929723501205, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.006643157918006182, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.003848279593512416, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.003118770429864526, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.002784608630463481, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0006719339289702475, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3226040, 'end': 3249552}, 'sentences_idx_start': 303, 'sentences_idx_end': 304}, {'text': "Which means that not only is a certain kind of dynamics instantiated, which make, for example, in the case of major depressive disorder, extremely negative self evaluations very common, but it's the case that even given the correct changes in environmental context. Even given in the case of psychedelic cystotherapy, a lot of the work with major depressive disorder is being done with treatment resistant depression, right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.986381471157074, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.026738757267594337, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.026665568351745605, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.021504273638129234, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.014863327145576477, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.01132415421307087, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004399995785206556, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0038642080035060644, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0032510077580809593, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.003098400542512536, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3249636, 'end': 3276868}, 'sentences_idx_start': 305, 'sentences_idx_end': 306}, {'text': 'And what is treatment resistant depression but a kind of a set of beliefs, a set of neural activity patterns which are resistant to adaptation, to new environmental contexts being whatever sort of psychotherapy or previous drug was used. So this is high plasticity loss, high overhead and rate and these are kind of fortunately for psychedelic therapy and I think maybe for psychiatry in general, these are all very common and very, very costly psychopathologies. Right?', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.978477418422699, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0558926984667778, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.03774598613381386, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.034154150635004044, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.024348607286810875, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.012248755432665348, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.006639128550887108, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.0020059365779161453, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0019123746315017343, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0018651861464604735, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3276954, 'end': 3311500}, 'sentences_idx_start': 307, 'sentences_idx_end': 309}, {'text': "So if it is the case that psychedelic therapy can treat these effectively, that's fantastic. But I think we can maybe look at a more complicated if we start to expand to other psychopathologies, the story becomes a little bit more complicated. Right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8982929587364197, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.2616664469242096, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.08040374517440796, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.03888155147433281, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.016980191692709923, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.014589959755539894, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.011286797001957893, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.009501442313194275, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005131381563842297, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0011943140998482704, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3311570, 'end': 3326244}, 'sentences_idx_start': 310, 'sentences_idx_end': 312}, {'text': "So we can look at the bottom left hand corner here where we have cases of in the inference landscape still overfitting, but in the learning landscape something else happening, form of kind of catastrophic forgetting or a form of kind of drift of the belief landscape that's being instantiated here. Right? So I think two kind of representative pathologies here typically referred to as some form of bipolar disorder or some form of borderline personality disorder.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.15584464371204376, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.03582068160176277, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.034424539655447006, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.017966412007808685, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.01601315848529339, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.010210624895989895, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.006572582293301821, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.006190953776240349, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.00400835694745183, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.002273865044116974, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3326442, 'end': 3360712}, 'sentences_idx_start': 313, 'sentences_idx_end': 315}, {'text': 'So in both of these cases, in the moment to moment neural activity as it unfolds, there are very strong sets of beliefs being instantiated at any given time and these are very difficult to change. Right? But the key differentiating point here being that over longer timescales, over the timescales of days or weeks, the kinds of beliefs that are instantiated change quite a lot. Right?', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6011475324630737, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.17452925443649292, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.03320218250155449, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.018402470275759697, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.006276174448430538, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00522068003192544, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.0024552319664508104, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0019280583364889026, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0015402400167658925, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0013520939974114299, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3360856, 'end': 3384484}, 'sentences_idx_start': 316, 'sentences_idx_end': 319}, {'text': "So someone who's bipolar, if they're in a manic episode or in a depressive episode, the nature of the belief landscape being instantiated is very different for borderline individuals from a daily or weekly basis, the nature of one's beliefs about the people that are close to them can change very rapidly, very extremely in certain cases.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8095056414604187, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.13017790019512177, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.10866902768611908, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.016180722042918205, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.013646716251969337, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.006582564674317837, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.002985717263072729, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.002839170629158616, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0026778331957757473, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0013853037962689996, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3384522, 'end': 3405180}, 'sentences_idx_start': 320, 'sentences_idx_end': 320}, {'text': "And so here the benefit of psychedelic therapy is a bit more mixed where there is likely the case that to the extent to which the kind of overt type A beliefs can be updated and changed to be more positive, be hopefully more relaxed, that's positive. But to the extent to which plasticity may be being increased when it's not actually needed, when there's not actually meaningful therapeutic benefits of that, it's a bit questionable.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9535366296768188, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.8144603967666626, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.2418627291917801, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.20550820231437683, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0878266841173172, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.02751016989350319, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005631271284073591, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004056708887219429, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.0036296644248068333, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.0032734349370002747, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3406480, 'end': 3439572}, 'sentences_idx_start': 321, 'sentences_idx_end': 322}, {'text': "I think there's clear borderline, or rather bipolar for example, is often individuals with bipolar are often excluded from psychedelic trials under the assumption for example, that psychedelics may trigger a manic episode or may trigger psychosis. And I think that is a valid concern. So on kind of that topic then, this bottom right hand corner would be cases of both underfooting and catastrophic forgetting with I think schizophrenia being kind of like the most clear manifestation of this.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5281097888946533, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.11552980542182922, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.08991244435310364, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.03959226980805397, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.011022938415408134, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.006868729833513498, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0034709477331489325, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.002610444091260433, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0023025856353342533, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0008398126810789108, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3439636, 'end': 3475670}, 'sentences_idx_start': 323, 'sentences_idx_end': 325}, {'text': "And here there's very little work currently looking at trying to treat schizophrenia with psychedelic therapy. I think for pretty good reasons though I would say to the extent to which there are secondary manifestations, secondary issues like depression, anxiety that people with schizophrenia might have, these actually may be treatable with some form of psychedelic therapy. And then lastly, this upper right hand corner here would correspond to underfitting in the type A landscape along with plasticity loss.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9871195554733276, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.07434479147195816, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.04605701565742493, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.02231159806251526, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 