elevance': 0.0036416780203580856, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3518652, 'end': 3557740}, 'sentences_idx_start': 329, 'sentences_idx_end': 332}, {'text': "Right, and then what would microdosing be doing? Right, microdosing would be very slowly kind of like decreasing plasticity loss just a little bit, potentially also decreasing underfitting, as Adam has kind of suggested in the Albus model. And here we have just kind of like a brief overview of more or less everything I've described about how these two landscapes are different. I think most of these things I've said before pretty clearly right so the type A landscape corresponds to the neural activity pattern.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.18367168307304382, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.005393254105001688, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0033955618273466825, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0018626836827024817, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>ThyroidDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0012091294629499316, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0006102473707869649, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0005133821978233755, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0005079580005258322, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.00046192234731279314, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.00038487554411403835, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3557810, 'end': 3596674}, 'sentences_idx_start': 333, 'sentences_idx_end': 336}, {'text': "This is the hidden state of the RNN. Overcannilization is going to be stereotyped mental circuits, very strongly held beliefs. Under canalization is going to be these inconsistently deployed circuits. It looks like overfitting in the canalized case, underfitting in the non canalized case going to correspond to stability, the metatrate. I hadn't discussed this before, but I think there's a relationship between cognitive flexibility and this inference landscape psychedelics are mainly going to affect the work at the acute level care.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.44798123836517334, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.1420750766992569, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.07028750330209732, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.017645075917243958, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.013348313048481941, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.007262729108333588, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0072571937926113605, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.00437281234189868, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.002117076190188527, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.001699229353107512, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3596722, 'end': 3632820}, 'sentences_idx_start': 337, 'sentences_idx_end': 341}, {'text': 'And this is by directly exciting the neurons or inducing forms of hadavian plasticity and the outcome is going to be a mixture of relaxation and strengthening of the kind that Adam described in the Albus case. The type B landscape then is working on the synaptic weights and these are the actual network parameters in our RNN model. Over canalization is this inability to learn or adapt over time. Under canalization is the inability to retain information right? And those correspond to plasticity loss and catastrophic forgetting.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.22445181012153625, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.011109030805528164, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.003315626410767436, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.001991622382774949, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008751144632697105, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0006679571233689785, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0006585944793187082, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.000562002940569073, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.00046632791054435074, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.00021419815311674029, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>ThyroidDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3633190, 'end': 3665870}, 'sentences_idx_start': 342, 'sentences_idx_end': 346}, {'text': "This also is kind of the traditional plasticity metatrate, which I think corresponds to this longer term constructed psychological flexibility. The effects are going to mainly be mediated post acutely with psychedelics and these are the more downstream metaplastic effects, the psychoplastogenic effects. And I think on the whole the effect here is a relaxation of canalization. And yeah, these are just the references. So those are the slides I have that's kind of the overview of the Deep canals model, I think.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.11315198242664337, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.024684496223926544, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.022187698632478714, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01804671809077263, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.01588675007224083, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.01191629096865654, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.006553405895829201, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.004290462471544743, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.003261758014559746, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.001961845438927412, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3666930, 'end': 3708362}, 'sentences_idx_start': 347, 'sentences_idx_end': 351}, {'text': "Now I'll turn it over to Mike who's going to share some thoughts both about this work and some of his own work and kind of this approach to understanding psychedelics more broadly. Ah, great. Yeah, thank you for that overview. That was great.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.19849875569343567, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.10866306722164154, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.10012681782245636, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.08388389647006989, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.021764514967799187, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.020797986537218094, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.014152586460113525, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.00953647866845131, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}, {'relevance': 0.008468518033623695, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.00309412507340312, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3708416, 'end': 3731060}, 'sentences_idx_start': 352, 'sentences_idx_end': 355}, {'text': "So I guess I'm just in general very optimistic about this corner of neuroscience, that there are these very intuitive models that are very sort of clinically significant and I also think there is a lot of responsibility to sort of get things right here as well. As Adam noted. I have just a few comments and for the viewers, I'm not speaking for Arthur and Adam, I'm just grateful for the invitation to join the discussion.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9886162877082825, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.05876707658171654, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.024631507694721222, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.009801163338124752, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.009389054961502552, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.00739280367270112, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.0050488668493926525, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.003898481372743845, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0036635971628129482, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.003294756170362234, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3733030, 'end': 3775330}, 'sentences_idx_start': 356, 'sentences_idx_end': 358}, {'text': 'So I wanted to note quickly three research themes dealing with the implementation of this class of model. So just broadly kind of pointing at both Deep Canals and Andrebus and Albus. So in 2019 I wrote Neural Annealing and that was sort of developing the canalization frame within the context of energy buildup in the eigen modes of a system. So you have the nice annealing metaphor, you have a temperature parameter and entropic disintegration.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9018523097038269, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.09904015064239502, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.01571657508611679, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002952319337055087, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0024614634457975626, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0018341874238103628, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006147487438283861, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0003409699711482972, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0002822054084390402, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0002712425193749368, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3777110, 'end': 3823710}, 'sentences_idx_start': 359, 'sentences_idx_end': 362}, {'text': "Robin Carter said a beautiful paper on that dantropic brain and then you sort of have a post heating result where the microstructure of your system is sort of a result of how hot and how long the heating was. So it's an alternative take on belief relaxation. And I do think that there are some pluses in terms of sort of explicitly making the annealing metaphor. And I think that two things that I'd point out.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.21759144961833954, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.08375635743141174, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.05447986349463463, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.047423556447029114, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.021347612142562866, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.012379912659525871, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.0035955391358584166, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.003051434876397252, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0021382335107773542, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0013735702959820628, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3825670, 'end': 3872846}, 'sentences_idx_start': 363, 'sentences_idx_end': 366}, {'text': 'One, top down models or top down predictive models as energy sinks and eigen modes as the places where energy can build up or almost sort of hide from top down models. So you get this phenomenon of semantically neutral energy or semantically illegible energy we can say, which is sort of kind of how perhaps psychedelics music and meditation all sort of allow energy building. The energy that they contribute to the system can evade the top tone models.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.037043627351522446, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.016334841027855873, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.006275541614741087, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0038741505704820156, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.002517059212550521, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0019384550396353006, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>Inspirational/NewAgeMusic'}, {'relevance': 0.00122702750377357, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0010977257043123245, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.001018228242173791, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008685861830599606, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3872948, 'end': 3910010}, 'sentences_idx_start': 367, 'sentences_idx_end': 369}, {'text': "And yeah, just to note, one item that I'm looking at now is what is Deep Canals? Has the inference landscape versus learning landscape distinction? And how would one sort of build that distinction within the neural Annealing framework? And guess one metaphor that I'm considering is the self as sort of a magnet to sort of apply a constraint, a uniform focusing constraint on the system as it's cooling.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6688464283943176, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.04157291352748871, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.009316550567746162, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.003564351238310337, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0008071490447036922, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007305796025320888, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007281901780515909, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006218952476046979, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005721887573599815, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0005045557045377791, 'label': 'Science'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3911710, 'end': 3946710}, 'sentences_idx_start': 370, 'sentences_idx_end': 373}, {'text': "The second item that I wanted to mention, so I have this piece, autism as a disorder of dimensionality. And this brings in the concept of network density that it may very well be that people on the spectrum have literally more neurons and or more synapses. And there's this great Michelangelo quote, I saw the angel in the stone, and I set him free. And sort of the thicker networks you have, the more stone you have to work with, but you actually have to do the work.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9861634373664856, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.03351103141903877, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.01134192943572998, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.010305489413440228, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.004438119940459728, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.002800026908516884, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.0023472087923437357, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0017873350298032165, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0014909917954355478, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0014749524416401982, 'label': 'FineArt'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3948570, 'end': 3985860}, 'sentences_idx_start': 374, 'sentences_idx_end': 377}, {'text': "So you sort of have to do sort of well, normally you sort of inherit these highly pretrained optimized circuits, almost like asics application specific integrated circuit. And then this is kind of more an untrained network, and you have to train it yourself. And within the Deep Canals framework, this would show up as both underfitting and higher capacity for plasticity. So I think that's going to be an interesting thread to pull. Finally.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.1391352266073227, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.12597644329071045, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.006786954589188099, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0012896365951746702, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0009968954836949706, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0008305518422275782, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0008133084629662335, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006717453361488879, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005233474657870829, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0003147315583191812, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3986470, 'end': 4031010}, 'sentences_idx_start': 378, 'sentences_idx_end': 382}, {'text': "So I just posted that last week, principles of Vaso Computation and as an implementation level account of active inference. And this is a big rabbit hole. I don't think we have time to go down it today. But I just comment that I really like the way Deep Canals explicitly splits out the learning landscape and the inference landscape, that I think that making this distinction is increasingly going to make sense. Back to Arthur. Yeah, awesome. Well, thank you all for the presentations.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.24748928844928741, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0055243270471692085, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.004270066507160664, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.003943377640098333, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.002050653798505664, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0020468728616833687, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.001786528737284243, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0015179378679022193, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008167085470631719, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.000582740583922714, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4031160, 'end': 4075900}, 'sentences_idx_start': 383, 'sentences_idx_end': 389}, {'text': "Arthur and Adam, feel free to pick up where Michael left off, or I can bring in some questions from the chat or from what I've written down. Just a quick comment. I do think that in the Deep Canals framework, it's 