 382344, 'confidence': 0.99994, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'likely', 'start': 382382, 'end': 382772, 'confidence': 0.99992, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'of', 'start': 382836, 'end': 383256, 'confidence': 0.67, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'central', 'start': 383358, 'end': 383764, 'confidence': 0.98376, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'importance', 'start': 383812, 'end': 384436, 'confidence': 0.93453, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'to', 'start': 384548, 'end': 384824, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'the', 'start': 384862, 'end': 385016, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'psychedelic', 'start': 385038, 'end': 385556, 'confidence': 0.99136, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'effect.', 'start': 385588, 'end': 386170, 'confidence': 0.99981, 'speaker': 'C'}]}, {'text': "So kind of moving up one level of abstraction to fMRI studies, there are a few kind of like key takeaways which have been identified from a few different fMRI studies looking at psychedelic use. Kind of the main theme has largely been this idea of increased entropy or increased complexity of the cortical activation in the brain. So there are various measures of this. On the right here there's a figure of one of the common measures of complexity and looking at various different kinds of states that an individual might be in and how that relates to complexity. So you have individuals in vegetative states or anesthesized states having relatively low brain activity complexity, you have individuals in awake states having higher complexity and then individuals who have ingested either psilocybin or LSD showing the highest brain complexity.", 'start': 390080, 'end': 460340, 'confidence': 0.99494, 'words': [{'text': 'So', 'start': 390080, 'end': 390504, 'confidence': 0.99494, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'kind', 'start': 390562, 'end': 390688, 'confidence': 0.99497, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'of', 'start': 390694, 'end': 390816, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'moving', 'start': 390838, 'end': 391072,