gance to it. In our deep Pinal's work that we've worked on, we kind of identify a couple of limitations of this canal model and attempt to extend and refine the model in ways that I think ultimately make it more powerful, while kind of keeping the essential elegant insight that cannibalization is kind of like intimately tied to pathology. So the first kind of limitation I think that we identify is that in the canal model it's very heavily implied that all forms of canalization are pathological in one way or another. And as I mentioned just now, this is clearly the case for a large class of very common psychopathologies. It's when we start to look more towards edge cases, I think that these exceptions start to problematize this understanding, right?", 'start': 1104660, 'end': 1172410, 'confidence': 0.99448, 'words': [{'text': 'So', 'start': 1104660, 'end': 1105072, 'confidence': 0.99448, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'I', 'start': 1105126, 'end': 1105296, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'think', 'start': 1105318, 'end': 1105456, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'this', 'start': 1105478, 'end': 1105664, 'confidence': 0.99999, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'work', 'start': 1105702, 'end': 1105904, 'confidence': 0.9999, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'has', 'start': 1105942, 'end': 1106192, 'confidence': 0.99996, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'a', 'start': 1106246, 'end': 1106368, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'lot', 'start': 1106374, 'end': 1106496, 'confidence': 0.98581, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'of', 'start': 1106518, 'end': 1106656, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'strengths', 'start': 1106678, 'end': 1107448, 'confidence': 0.80821, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'and', 'start': 1107564, 'end': 1107988, 'confidence': 0.99, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': "there's", 'start': 1108074, 'end': 1108416, 'confidence': 0.99905, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'a', 'start': 1108448, 'end': 1108548, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'kind', 'st